    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Idris I, a great-grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-ali">Hasan ibn Ali</a>, fled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fakhkh">Battle of Fakhkh</a> and was made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awraba">Awraba</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volubilis">Volubilis</a> in 788.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-ii">Idris II</a> moved his seat to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> in 809 and welcomed Arab settlers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 818 and from Aghlabid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunisia">Tunisia</a> in 824, giving the city its Arab character.</li><li>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-ii">Idris II</a>'s death in 828 the realm was divided among his sons; the Idrisids lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> for good in 927 and were removed from power by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyads</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> in 974.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Idris I left no male heir when an Abbasid agent poisoned him in 791, but his wife Lalla Kanza bore his only son shortly after his death; the boy, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-ii">Idris II</a>, was proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awraba">Awraba</a> at the age of eleven.</p></aside>
    </section>

