bers</a> make him their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">791</span><span class="rf-text">Idris I is poisoned by an Abbasid agent; his posthumous son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-ii">Idris II</a> is brought up under the regency of the freedman Rashid.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">809</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-ii">Idris II</a> has the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awraba">Awraba</a> leader Ishak killed and moves his seat from Walili to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>, founding the settlement of al-'Aliya.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">828</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idris-ii">Idris II</a> dies; the state reaches from western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sous">Sous</a>, and his son Muhammad divides it among seven brothers.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">836–863</span><span class="rf-text">Ali ibn Muhammad and Yahya I rule in stability; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qarawiyyin-mosque">al-Qarawiyyin</a> and al-Andalusiyyin mosques are founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">868</span><span class="rf-text">The Sufri Kharijite tribes of Madyuna, Ghayata and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miknasa">Miknasa</a> defeat Ali ibn Umar and occupy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a> until Yahya III retakes it.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">927</span><span class="rf-text">Musa ibn Abul 'Afiya of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miknasa">Miknasa</a> captures and kills Hassan I al-Hajam: the Idrisids never again hold <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fez">Fez</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">974</span><span class="rf-text">The Umayyad general Ghalib expels the I